T1  - Ability of Nontraditional Risk Factors and Inflammatory Biomarkers for Cardiovascular Disease to Identify High Cardiometabolic Risk in Adolescents: Results From the LabMed Physical Activity Study.
DO  - https://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.jadohealth.2017.09.012
A1  - Agostinis-Sobrinho, Cesar
A1  - Ruiz, Jonatan R
A1  - Moreira, Carla
A1  - Abreu, Sandra
