T1  - Changes in carotid artery sonogram in premature adrenarche.
DO  - https://dx.doi.org/10.1515/jpem.2011.411
A1  - Mathew, Revi P
A1  - Hernanz-Schulman, Marta
A1  - Wang, Wenli
A1  - Saville, Benjamin
A1  - Bremer, Andrew
Y1  - 2012//
N2  - <ovid:b>BACKGROUND</ovid:b>: Premature adrenarche (PA), the appearance of pubic hair before the age of 8 years in girls and before 9 years in boys, may predict future morbidity, such as metabolic syndrome (MS)., <ovid:b>OBJECTIVE</ovid:b>: The purpose of this study is to assess carotid artery ultrasound changes in children with PA., <ovid:b>DESIGN/METHODS</ovid:b>: PA children were matched with a group of prepubertal controls without PA. Subjects and controls underwent clinical and biochemical evaluation and sonograms of the carotid arteries., <ovid:b>RESULTS</ovid:b>: Twelve children with PA and their matched controls were studied. Carotid artery ultrasonography showed elevation of the inner and outer diameter of the left carotid, and the cross-sectional area of the lumen and outer wall, and the outer diameter of the right carotid artery in PA. However, none of the above results maintained statistical significance when a Hochberg correction was applied., <ovid:b>CONCLUSIONS</ovid:b>: Carotid artery diameter and cross-sectional area may be useful non-invasive markers of vascular pathology and MS in premature pubarche.
